WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:37.880
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:38.150 --> 01:43.900
[Small Town Remedy]

3
01:44.110 --> 01:46.890
[Episode 12]

4
01:48.229 --> 01:48.590
Okay.

5
01:56.310 --> 01:57.560
Why am I at your place?

6
01:57.759 --> 01:58.920
They all went home.

7
01:58.920 --> 02:00.780
I have to take care of you, don't I?

8
02:01.400 --> 02:02.560
I told Zhengguang

9
02:02.560 --> 02:03.960
to pick you up after work.

10
02:04.280 --> 02:05.590
Did I embarrass myself?

11
02:05.590 --> 02:06.400
Yes.

12
02:11.560 --> 02:13.360
Getting drunk is a sign of respect for the alcohol,

13
02:13.360 --> 02:14.030
right?

14
02:14.840 --> 02:15.680
But

15
02:16.230 --> 02:18.710
it also depends on your constitution.

16
02:18.870 --> 02:20.800
You seem to lack that...

17
02:21.150 --> 02:22.750
What do experts call it?

18
02:22.750 --> 02:23.430
That...

19
02:23.430 --> 02:24.310
Acetaldehyde dehydrogenase

20
02:24.310 --> 02:25.910
and alcohol dehydrogenase.

21
02:26.190 --> 02:27.000
What's that?

22
02:29.150 --> 02:30.310
It's some enzymes in everyone's body

23
02:30.310 --> 02:32.630
needed to break down alcohol.

24
02:35.560 --> 02:36.820
It basically means...

25
02:37.030 --> 02:39.690
You don't seem like someone from the Northeast.

26
02:47.120 --> 02:49.380
I'm not from the Northeast to begin with.

27
02:50.310 --> 02:51.310
Why do you have to be

28
02:51.310 --> 02:52.840
so annoying when you speak?

29
03:05.800 --> 03:06.750
If only I hadn't come over

30
03:06.750 --> 03:08.210
to eat noodles that night.

31
03:09.310 --> 03:12.510
There might still be a glimmer of hope for resuscitation.

32
03:24.840 --> 03:25.960
In all my years in the funeral business,

33
03:25.960 --> 03:27.190
I've seen it all.

34
03:28.680 --> 03:29.750
Who can say

35
03:29.750 --> 03:31.870
when someone will die or live?

36
03:34.000 --> 03:34.840
Sometimes,

37
03:36.630 --> 03:37.750
the family notifies us,

38
03:37.750 --> 03:39.190
saying the person has passed away,

39
03:39.190 --> 03:41.720
and we should hurry up and make arrangements.

40
03:41.960 --> 03:44.160
Then they suddenly catch their breath.

41
03:47.710 --> 03:48.430
Really.

42
03:50.710 --> 03:52.030
But there are also those

43
03:52.030 --> 03:53.120
who usually

44
03:53.400 --> 03:54.520
look very healthy,

45
03:55.079 --> 03:56.740
with nothing wrong with them,

46
03:56.840 --> 03:58.240
but suddenly,

47
04:00.630 --> 04:01.840
they're just gone.

48
04:08.910 --> 04:10.030
So before,

49
04:10.030 --> 04:11.430
I also wondered about it.

50
04:12.190 --> 04:14.390
But death doesn't discriminate by age.

51
04:15.680 --> 04:16.480
You

52
04:18.160 --> 04:19.820
treat the sick and save lives.

53
04:21.040 --> 04:21.600
And I

54
04:22.950 --> 04:24.560
help those who can't be cured

55
04:25.190 --> 04:26.920
leave this world with dignity.

56
04:29.070 --> 04:30.720
We just do our best.

57
04:32.870 --> 04:35.360
As for when a person actually leaves,

58
04:36.600 --> 04:38.510
that's for the King of Hell to figure out,

59
04:38.510 --> 04:39.270
right?

60
05:03.040 --> 05:04.430
That hot and sour soup

61
05:04.680 --> 05:05.950
is really good for a hangover.

62
05:05.950 --> 05:06.720
Is that so?

63
05:07.190 --> 05:08.560
I'm much more sober now.

64
05:09.830 --> 05:10.630
Thank you.

65
05:11.750 --> 05:13.680
Running away as soon as you wake up?

66
05:31.040 --> 05:31.750
Jie.

67
05:34.310 --> 05:36.040
Is your probation period over?

68
05:37.270 --> 05:39.530
Do you want to become a regular employee?

69
05:39.920 --> 05:41.510
I don't think I will.

70
05:41.510 --> 05:42.240
Why?

71
05:42.800 --> 05:44.330
Do you look down on our work?

72
05:44.800 --> 05:45.750
No, Jie.

73
05:45.800 --> 05:47.460
I absolutely don't mean that.

74
05:48.720 --> 05:50.950
Do you think you can just leave whenever you want?

75
05:50.950 --> 05:52.240
What do you think

76
05:52.240 --> 05:53.640
our Blossom & Fortune is?

77
05:57.480 --> 05:58.800
What do you mean, Jie?

78
06:01.310 --> 06:02.950
We have to see you off.

79
06:04.950 --> 06:10.510
♪ Beyond the pavilion, beside the ancient road ♪

80
06:10.510 --> 06:15.040
♪ Green grass stretches to the horizon ♪

81
06:15.480 --> 06:20.720
♪ The evening breeze brushes the willows, and the flute's notes fade away ♪

82
06:20.800 --> 06:24.830
♪ The setting sun sinks beyond range upon range of mountains ♪

83
06:24.830 --> 06:25.630
Stop!

84
06:27.240 --> 06:27.970
Don't laugh.

85
06:31.160 --> 06:31.950
Well.

86
06:35.040 --> 06:36.190
Following an unreliable boss,

87
06:36.190 --> 06:37.430
I got infected a bit.

88
06:39.120 --> 06:39.920
You're right.

89
06:40.270 --> 06:41.930
You really don't belong here.

90
06:42.920 --> 06:44.360
You don't know how to

91
06:44.870 --> 06:46.470
find joy in sorrow like we do.

92
06:51.920 --> 06:53.480
Your shop is quite big.

93
06:53.870 --> 06:55.330
Do you usually live alone?

94
06:58.000 --> 06:59.830
I stay in the shop on Mondays, Wednesdays, and Fridays.

95
06:59.830 --> 07:03.090
I go home on Tuesdays, Thursdays, Saturdays, and Sundays.

96
07:04.680 --> 07:05.390
Such a big place.

97
07:05.390 --> 07:07.190
Aren't you scared living alone?

98
07:07.560 --> 07:09.160
What's there to be scared of?

99
07:10.000 --> 07:11.720
The ones you find scary

100
07:12.390 --> 07:13.920
are the ones many people yearn for day and night

101
07:13.920 --> 07:15.630
but can never see.

102
07:22.240 --> 07:23.680
Last time you came to the hospital to see me,

103
07:23.680 --> 07:24.480
you told me

104
07:24.720 --> 07:26.390
you had that condition where you get dizzy

105
07:26.390 --> 07:27.190
when you read.

106
07:28.920 --> 07:29.980
I was just kidding.

107
07:32.240 --> 07:32.970
That's good.

108
07:42.159 --> 07:43.360
What's good about it?

109
07:46.630 --> 07:48.760
It's always good to not be sick, right?

110
07:54.630 --> 07:56.630
If I really had that condition,

111
07:57.920 --> 07:59.120
could you cure me?

112
08:05.040 --> 08:05.680
Yes!

113
08:07.040 --> 08:08.070
My KTV career

114
08:08.070 --> 08:09.190
is finally over!

115
08:09.950 --> 08:10.750
That's great!

116
08:18.440 --> 08:20.800
[1314 Funeral Supplies, Xiaoximen Store]

117
08:19.120 --> 08:19.920
I'm leaving.

118
08:20.480 --> 08:21.310
Get lost.

119
08:21.600 --> 08:22.390
Sis.

120
08:22.750 --> 08:24.430
What time do you open tomorrow?

121
08:24.430 --> 08:25.720
I'll come over and help out.

122
08:25.210 --> 08:28.020
[1314 Funeral Supplies, Xiaoximen Store]

123
08:26.240 --> 08:27.070
Why are you coming?

124
08:27.070 --> 08:28.120
Didn't you quit?

125
08:29.240 --> 08:30.390
I still feel that

126
08:30.390 --> 08:31.510
selling urns suits me.

127
08:31.510 --> 08:33.270
I was thinking of coming back to continue working.

128
08:33.270 --> 08:34.270
Come on.

129
08:34.630 --> 08:35.270
You're past the age

130
08:35.270 --> 08:36.669
of selling urns.

131
08:36.870 --> 08:37.510
No.

132
08:38.360 --> 08:39.960
Does selling urns have an age limit?

133
08:39.960 --> 08:41.240
Sis, what are you talking about?

134
08:41.240 --> 08:41.909
Besides,

135
08:42.270 --> 08:43.510
my previous performance

136
08:43.510 --> 08:44.480
was pretty good, wasn't it?

137
08:44.480 --> 08:45.120
Yes.

138
08:45.360 --> 08:46.120
But aren't you going

139
08:46.120 --> 08:47.630
to Beijing to develop your career?

140
08:47.630 --> 08:48.890
Our place is too small.

141
08:50.750 --> 08:51.550
Beijing...

142
08:51.670 --> 08:53.270
I haven't made up my mind yet.

143
08:53.870 --> 08:55.130
What's wrong with you?

144
08:55.750 --> 08:57.210
You've become a stray dog?

145
08:57.870 --> 08:58.630
You don't know what to do,

146
08:58.630 --> 09:00.440
so you come to me for a place to stay, right?

147
09:00.440 --> 09:02.270
But if you admit you're a stray dog,

148
09:02.270 --> 09:03.530
I can let you come back.

149
09:04.120 --> 09:05.520
But I don't think you are.

150
09:07.390 --> 09:08.200
See?

151
09:07.780 --> 09:10.310
[1314 Funeral Supplies — at your service]

152
09:09.030 --> 09:10.490
Once this thing is posted,

153
09:10.750 --> 09:11.910
many people come.

154
09:10.910 --> 09:11.810
[Hiring]

155
09:11.910 --> 09:12.840
I have no choice.

156
09:12.840 --> 09:13.550
This thing...

157
09:13.550 --> 09:14.790
One person per position.

158
09:14.790 --> 09:15.720
-Sis. -So, look.

159
09:15.720 --> 09:16.960
Now there's no position for you.

160
09:16.960 --> 09:18.390
If you really love this industry,

161
09:18.390 --> 09:19.630
go check out other places.

162
09:19.630 --> 09:20.320
Sis.

163
09:20.380 --> 09:23.210
[Funeral Wreaths and Burial Clothing]

164
09:20.510 --> 09:22.110
You're kidding, right, sis?

165
09:22.150 --> 09:23.080
Liu Zhengguang,

166
09:24.030 --> 09:25.290
are you leaving or not?

167
09:25.840 --> 09:26.720
Sir, wait a moment.

168
09:26.720 --> 09:27.870
I'm leaving, sis!

169
09:29.550 --> 09:30.390
Hurry up.

170
09:30.750 --> 09:31.550
Get in.

171
09:32.220 --> 09:36.330
[Fucheng City Taxi]

172
09:46.790 --> 09:47.720
Liu Zhengliang,

173
09:50.750 --> 09:52.910
do you think I can find a job in Beijing?

174
09:54.000 --> 09:54.960
How would I know?

175
09:58.240 --> 09:59.870
If I don't go to Beijing,

176
10:00.600 --> 10:02.390
what am I supposed to do here?

177
10:03.840 --> 10:04.960
I don't know.

178
10:08.670 --> 10:10.510
Then tell me how I can

179
10:10.670 --> 10:13.200
cross the vast sea of suffering

180
10:13.270 --> 10:16.390
and reach the shore of enlightenment?

181
10:17.840 --> 10:18.960
I want to know too.

182
10:21.600 --> 10:23.480
Sir, what are you laughing at?

183
10:24.840 --> 10:26.870
It's funny hearing you two young guys

184
10:26.870 --> 10:28.960
use such profound words.

185
10:31.600 --> 10:32.390
Sir,

186
10:32.550 --> 10:33.270
driving a taxi,

187
10:33.270 --> 10:34.870
how much can you earn a month?

188
10:35.550 --> 10:37.480
Just enough to support the family.

189
10:37.790 --> 10:39.450
I don't eat big chunks of meat,

190
10:39.510 --> 10:40.630
and I can't wear brand-name clothes.

191
10:40.630 --> 10:42.030
It shouldn't be that bad, sir.

192
10:42.030 --> 10:43.150
The cost of living in Fucheng

193
10:43.150 --> 10:43.910
is so low.

194
10:44.000 --> 10:46.750
The cost of living in Fucheng is low,

195
10:47.080 --> 10:48.160
but my kid

196
10:48.190 --> 10:50.390
is studying at a university in Beijing.

197
10:51.670 --> 10:53.270
What I earn alone

198
10:53.270 --> 10:54.930
is not enough for him to spend.

199
10:55.150 --> 10:56.150
Now,

200
10:56.510 --> 10:58.790
I just hope he graduates quickly

201
10:58.790 --> 10:59.960
and starts working.

202
11:00.870 --> 11:01.630
Every month,

203
11:01.630 --> 11:04.290
as long as he doesn't ask me for money, it's fine.

204
11:04.790 --> 11:06.240
So is he staying in Beijing

205
11:06.240 --> 11:07.360
or coming back?

206
11:07.910 --> 11:09.270
I asked him twice,

207
11:09.390 --> 11:10.080
but this brat

208
11:10.080 --> 11:11.880
won't give me a straight answer.

209
11:12.390 --> 11:14.990
According to the saying of our Fucheng people,

210
11:15.000 --> 11:16.230
for an old horse that knows the way,

211
11:16.230 --> 11:17.290
the route is clear.

212
11:17.750 --> 11:20.010
Coming home and getting an iron rice bowl

213
11:20.120 --> 11:21.650
is stable and respectable.

214
11:22.630 --> 11:25.000
A thousand-mile horse that has high aspirations

215
11:25.000 --> 11:27.840
will work hard in big cities like Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, or Shenzhen.

216
11:27.840 --> 11:29.170
What about a lost horse?

217
11:29.630 --> 11:30.790
Caught in a dilemma,

218
11:31.000 --> 11:32.240
sighing in despair.

219
11:33.440 --> 11:34.480
Today,

220
11:35.440 --> 11:37.000
it's either dogs or horses.

221
11:37.510 --> 11:38.320
Sir,

222
11:38.630 --> 11:40.790
we are humans, not horses.

223
11:41.390 --> 11:42.480
Right, humans.

224
11:55.320 --> 11:56.320
Sir, right here.

225
11:56.790 --> 11:57.600
Okay.

226
11:58.360 --> 11:59.150
Bro,

227
11:59.510 --> 12:01.170
remember what you said today.

228
12:01.240 --> 12:02.840
No matter how things turn out,

229
12:02.840 --> 12:04.770
you must treat yourself as a human.

230
12:05.120 --> 12:06.650
Advice from me, Ma (horse).

231
12:07.750 --> 12:08.510
Seven yuan.

232
12:08.510 --> 12:09.600
Cash or QR code?

233
12:09.840 --> 12:10.630
QR code.

234
12:15.870 --> 12:17.000
We're leaving, sir.

235
12:17.000 --> 12:17.630
Goodbye.

236
12:27.390 --> 12:28.630
Hello, please change the dressing.

237
12:28.630 --> 12:29.540
Okay, I'll do it.

238
12:29.540 --> 12:29.920
[Emergency Cart]

239
12:30.130 --> 12:34.200
[Emergency Cart]

240
12:32.870 --> 12:34.730
Where do you feel uncomfortable?

241
12:35.750 --> 12:37.030
I'm fifty-five.

242
12:38.270 --> 12:40.550
I used to be Chuizishan County's

243
12:40.550 --> 12:42.870
top turtle breeder.

244
12:47.790 --> 12:50.590
I'm proficient in Yin-Yang and the Five Elements.

245
12:50.790 --> 12:52.590
I'm asking what your illness is!

246
12:53.550 --> 12:54.480
I'm not sick!

247
12:55.870 --> 12:56.550
Doctor,

248
12:56.550 --> 12:57.720
my dad often has

249
12:57.720 --> 12:58.550
epileptic seizures.

250
12:58.550 --> 12:59.390
When he has a seizure,

251
12:59.390 --> 13:00.630
his whole body twitches,

252
13:00.630 --> 13:01.630
and he foams at the mouth.

253
13:01.630 --> 13:02.910
How long have these symptoms lasted?

254
13:02.910 --> 13:04.200
For five or six days.

255
13:06.720 --> 13:08.030
This is not an illness.

256
13:08.630 --> 13:10.670
It's an excess of Wood energy.

257
13:11.270 --> 13:13.800
Governing heavenly qi is Taiyang Cold Water,

258
13:13.910 --> 13:16.200
guest Qi is Yangming Dry Metal.

259
13:22.670 --> 13:23.200
Then

260
13:23.200 --> 13:24.200
I'll take his blood pressure first.

261
13:24.200 --> 13:25.120
Come, help him take off his clothes.

262
13:25.120 --> 13:25.600
Come.

263
13:28.000 --> 13:28.790
-Sis. -Yes?

264
13:29.360 --> 13:30.600
Are there any small paper coffins left?

265
13:30.600 --> 13:32.200
The ones at home are sold out.

266
13:32.320 --> 13:33.720
There should be two small ones left.

267
13:33.720 --> 13:35.270
Go check the loft bed.

268
13:35.270 --> 13:36.270
The loft bed, huh?

269
13:37.510 --> 13:39.170
These flowers are beautiful.

270
13:39.630 --> 13:41.440
Let's get some for our old shop.

271
13:41.870 --> 13:43.550
This is a different variety.

272
13:43.550 --> 13:44.120
Look.

273
13:44.120 --> 13:45.440
Flowers like hydrangeas

274
13:45.440 --> 13:46.670
and gentians,

275
13:47.030 --> 13:48.200
they look so nice for patients.

276
13:48.200 --> 13:49.260
Arrange them a bit,

277
13:49.510 --> 13:50.960
and they'll be very pretty.

278
13:50.960 --> 13:52.030
Our old shop

279
13:52.030 --> 13:54.510
only needs flowers suitable for funerals.

280
13:54.960 --> 13:55.960
Wholesale is fine.

281
13:55.960 --> 13:57.870
Who would go to a wreath shop

282
13:57.960 --> 13:59.560
to buy flowers for a patient?

283
13:59.600 --> 14:00.870
Aren't they afraid of bad luck?

284
14:00.870 --> 14:02.360
Giving flowers leaves a lingering fragrance.

285
14:02.360 --> 14:03.690
How could it be bad luck?

286
14:03.870 --> 14:04.440
Come on.

287
14:04.440 --> 14:07.080
If they think it's bad luck, I won't sell to them.

288
14:07.080 --> 14:07.870
Yesterday,

289
14:08.670 --> 14:09.930
Zhengguang came to me.

290
14:10.600 --> 14:12.200
He wants to come back to work.

291
14:12.320 --> 14:13.450
What? Did you agree?

292
14:14.030 --> 14:14.960
No.

293
14:15.870 --> 14:16.870
Didn't you tell me

294
14:16.910 --> 14:17.870
not to agree?

295
14:17.870 --> 14:19.000
Of course.

296
14:19.870 --> 14:22.000
Then why didn't you let him come back?

297
14:22.000 --> 14:23.390
He's in his twenties.

298
14:23.390 --> 14:24.270
He's been selling urns all this time.

299
14:24.270 --> 14:25.800
What kind of future is that?

300
14:27.270 --> 14:28.480
Have you found it?

301
14:28.870 --> 14:29.670
I haven't seen it.

302
14:29.670 --> 14:31.730
You have to let him go out and explore.

303
14:32.030 --> 14:33.430
He needs to make friends.

304
14:33.840 --> 14:35.360
Push the paper ingots in.

305
14:35.360 --> 14:36.690
It's all the way inside.

306
14:36.960 --> 14:38.840
Then last time he wanted to go to Beijing,

307
14:38.840 --> 14:40.500
why did you secretly stop him?

308
14:40.550 --> 14:41.670
Is that the same?

309
14:41.960 --> 14:42.960
It's fine to explore,

310
14:42.960 --> 14:44.150
but isn't the nearby area enough to make a go of it?

311
14:44.150 --> 14:45.750
Does he have to go to Beijing?

312
14:46.270 --> 14:47.600
As the saying goes,

313
14:47.630 --> 14:49.750
a tree won't grow straight without pruning,

314
14:49.750 --> 14:51.320
and a person won't be tough without a beating.

315
14:51.320 --> 14:51.840
Be careful.

316
14:51.840 --> 14:53.550
You've thought of everything.

317
14:53.550 --> 14:54.210
Be careful.

318
14:54.320 --> 14:55.790
Is there a smaller one?

319
14:56.240 --> 14:57.840
I think this is the smallest.

320
14:58.080 --> 14:59.200
Is this size not okay?

321
14:59.200 --> 15:00.200
How old is the deceased?

322
15:00.200 --> 15:01.000
Two...

323
15:01.910 --> 15:03.080
in fifteen days.

324
15:05.960 --> 15:06.750
Where is he?

325
15:07.320 --> 15:08.380
Across the street.

326
15:10.750 --> 15:11.720
I told you.

327
15:11.720 --> 15:12.960
What's the use?

328
15:13.750 --> 15:16.000
Since we came here,

329
15:16.200 --> 15:17.660
how many tests have we had?

330
15:18.270 --> 15:19.150
And they still haven't explained clearly

331
15:19.150 --> 15:20.510
the ins and outs of it.

332
15:20.550 --> 15:22.200
What disease is it exactly?

333
15:23.240 --> 15:24.840
Why don't we transfer to another hospital?

334
15:24.840 --> 15:26.440
Why waste that money?

335
15:26.600 --> 15:27.360
I've seen enough.

336
15:27.360 --> 15:28.790
Their medical skills

337
15:28.840 --> 15:29.630
are not even as good as my

338
15:29.630 --> 15:31.200
Yin-Yang Bagua therapy.

339
15:32.150 --> 15:33.360
If you don't trust us,

340
15:33.360 --> 15:34.960
you can transfer to No. 1 Hospital.

341
15:34.960 --> 15:36.080
Don't just go home like this,

342
15:36.080 --> 15:37.320
